{"sections":[],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems"]]},"metadata":{"title":"Scheduling Systems","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"role":"article"},"abstract":[{"text":"Order the systems of a schedule, run them only when a condition holds, and find out how a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schedule runs them.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Essentials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"],"title":"Essentials"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" lists the systems of one frame or step. When it runs, it decides the order from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"what you wrote and the constraints you added, and it runs the systems that can’t affect one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"another at the same time."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Order Systems","anchor":"Order-Systems","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems run in the order you write them, adjusted by ordering constraints. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" moves a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system after another, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" moves it before one; every other system keeps its written"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"place. A constraint that names a type with no system in the schedule is ignored. Constraints that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"form a cycle trap, and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(checked:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" throws "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" instead, for systems"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or constraints that come from configuration."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Run Systems Conditionally","anchor":"Run-Systems-Conditionally","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"runIf(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" skips a system unless a condition on the world holds, such as the world holding no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Paused"},{"type":"text","text":" resource. On a nested schedule, it applies to each of the nested schedule’s systems. Each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system checks its conditions at the start of the wave it runs in, so a system that changes what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a condition reads affects the systems in later waves. A condition must read only what each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system’s access lists."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Understand Waves","anchor":"Understand-Waves","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two systems "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"conflict","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" when one writes a type the other reads or writes, or when either has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" runs the systems in "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"waves","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": each wave holds the systems"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose earlier conflicting and ordered systems have run, and its systems run at the same time. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"commands systems queue apply when their wave finishes, so a system in the same wave doesn’t see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"another’s spawns, despawns or inserts. To see them, order it after the system that queued them."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The world ends as though the systems had run one after another, in order. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/runSerially(on:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"runs the same waves one system at a time, with the same result. Use it to step through a system in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a debugger, or to rule out running at the same time as the cause of a problem."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A system’s access comes from its parameters, with the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()"},{"type":"text","text":" macro, or from an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"access"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you declare by hand. A system without one may change anything, so it runs alone. In debug"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"builds, a system that reaches a type its access doesn’t list traps, so run a schedule’s tests in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"debug."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Find Unordered Conflicts","anchor":"Find-Unordered-Conflicts","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, the order they run in rests only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on how they happen to be written, which a later edit can change by accident.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()"},{"text":" lists those pairs. Order each pair, or mark it with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem\/ambiguous(with:)"},{"text":" when either order is right, and check in a test that the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"list stays empty.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Group Systems into Sets","anchor":"Group-Systems-into-Sets","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet"},{"text":" names a group of systems, so a constraint can refer to all of them at once.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Declare one as an empty enumeration. A system joins it with ","type":"text"},{"code":"inSet(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and a nested schedule","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"takes ","type":"text"},{"code":"inSet(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"after(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"before(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"runIf(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for all of its systems. Every system","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type is a set too, holding each system of that type.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The following schedule groups gravity and movement into a physics set that doesn’t run while","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the game is paused, and scores after every physics system:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let frame = Schedule {","    Schedule {","        Gravity()","        Movement().after(Gravity.self)","    }","    .inSet(Physics.self)","    .runIf { world in !world.resources.contains(Paused.self) }","    Scoring().after(Physics.self)","}","print(frame.names)","\/\/ Prints \"[\"Gravity\", \"Movement\", \"Scoring\"]\"","print(frame.ambiguities().isEmpty)","\/\/ Prints \"true\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","text":"Profile a Schedule","anchor":"Profile-a-Schedule","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Insert a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile"},{"text":" resource into a world, and every schedule that runs on it records each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system’s runs and times. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/writeDOT(to:)"},{"text":" writes a schedule’s dependency graph in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"DOT language, so Graphviz can draw why systems run in the order they do and which can run at the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same time.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems\/schedulingsystems"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Schedule","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/run(on:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/run(on:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"run"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"on"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"inout"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"World"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs each system once on a world, running systems that don’t depend on each other at the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same time."}],"title":"run(on:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ScheduledSystem/ambiguous(with:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ambiguous","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<each ","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"with","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": repeat (each ","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":").Type) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScheduledSystem","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems15ScheduledSystemV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"ambiguous(with:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/scheduledsystem\/ambiguous(with:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem\/ambiguous(with:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns this system, also free to run in either order with every system in each of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"given sets."}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/init(checked:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(checked:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/init(checked:)","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"checked","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems15ScheduledSystemV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ScheduledSystem"},{"kind":"text","text":"]) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems14CyclicOrderingV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"CyclicOrdering"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a schedule of the given systems, throwing an error if their ordering constraints"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"form a cycle."}],"title":"init(checked:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/runSerially(on:)":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"runSerially"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"on"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"World","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/runserially(on:)","title":"runSerially(on:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/runSerially(on:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs each system once on a world, one system at a time."}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/ambiguities()":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ambiguities","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems9AmbiguityV","text":"Ambiguity","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"ambiguities()","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns every pair of systems whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"orders."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/ambiguities()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemProfile":{"title":"SystemProfile","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemprofile","abstract":[{"text":"A resource that records how long each system takes to run.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/access":{"role":"symbol","required":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","defaultImplementations":1,"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"access"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6AccessV","text":"Access"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The component, resource and event types the system reads and writes, or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" if it may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change anything.","type":"text"}],"title":"access","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/access"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/drivingaworldfromanapp","title":"Driving a World from an App","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Hold a world in your app or game engine, feed it each frame’s input, and let the objects outside"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it read results and take part in a step."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemSet":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemSet","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemSet","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A type that names a group of systems, so ordering constraints can refer to all of them at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"once.","type":"text"}],"title":"SystemSet","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemset"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/CyclicOrdering":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CyclicOrdering"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CyclicOrdering"}],"title":"CyclicOrdering","abstract":[{"text":"An error indicating that the ordering constraints of a schedule’s systems form a cycle, so no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order satisfies them all.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/cyclicordering"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System()":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system()","kind":"symbol","title":"System()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"macro","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"System","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Makes a type a system whose access comes from the parameters of its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A rule that reads and changes a world, run once each time its schedule runs."}],"title":"System","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","url":"\/documentation\/systems","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"Systems","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/writeDOT(to:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/writedot(to:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"writeDOT"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"to"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"inout"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s16TextOutputStreamP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TextOutputStream"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/writeDOT(to:)","title":"writeDOT(to:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Writes the schedule’s dependency graph in the DOT language, for drawing with Graphviz."}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/DeclaringSystems":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/declaringsystems","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Declaring Systems","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Write the rules of a simulation as systems, and let their parameters state what they read and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"write."}],"kind":"article"}}}